AliasMode: behind a proxy without UDP (an HTTP proxy), show the ICE agent
stock Firefox on the identity's network shows instead of a machine whose UDP is
blocked: for every transport of the offer and every component of each, host
candidates, a srflx with the identity's address after the round trip through
the proxy from a STUN server that could answer, the errors and timings nICEr
gives the others, and checks that fail. None of it sends a packet. Behind a
SOCKS5 proxy with UDP the real agent works through the proxy's UDP relay
(webrtc-socks5-udp.patch) and this never starts. The choice follows the
context's proxy only, so every connection of a context shows the same network:
with a TURN server over TCP or TLS, which the real agent reaches through the
proxy, the real agent gathers for its relay candidate and checks, and this
gives the host candidates, the srflx and the errors, also when
media.peerconnection.ice.no_host hides the real agent's host candidates.
aliasmode:webrtcFakeIce false turns it off.

